ℕ and E⊆ℝ^n, if E is nonempty and compact, then for I=[0,1] and the concatenated Euclidean metric on E×I, dim_H(E×I)=dim_H(E)+1.\\\",\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"dim_H(E×I)=dim_H(E)+1.\\\",\\\"parameters\\\":[{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"n\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"nonnegative integer\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"E\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"subset of Euclidean ℝ^n\\\"}],\\\"hypotheses\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H001\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"E is nonempty.\\\",\\\"origin\\\":\\\"frozen-target.md:7-9\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H002\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"E is compact.\\\",\\\"origin\\\":\\\"frozen-target.md:7-9\\\"}],\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"logic\\\":{\\\"classical\\\":true,\\\"rules\\\":[\\\"case_elimination\\\",\\\"contradiction_classical\\\",\\\"direct\\\",\\\"exists_elimination\\\",\\\"forall_introduction\\\",\\\"implication_introduction\\\",\\\"modus_ponens\\\",\\\"natural_induction\\\",\\\"negation_introduction\\\"],\\\"calculations\\\":[\\\"Coordinate projections are 1-Lipschitz in the concatenated Euclidean metric. For subsets U⊆ℝ^n and J⊆ℝ, diam(U×J)≤√(diam(U)^2+diam(J)^2). Subdivide [0,1] into at most 1/r+1 intervals of length at most r when 0<r≤1.\\\"],\\\"primitives\\\":[{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"ℝ^n\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"Euclidean space of dimension n\\\",\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The n-dimensional real inner-product space, including the singleton ℝ^0.\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"dim_H\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"Hausdorff dimension\\\",\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"Critical exponent of Hausdorff measures, with empty-set dimension zero.\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"I\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"subset of ℝ\\\",\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The closed interval [0,1].\\\"}]},\\\"pins\\\":{\\\"lean_version\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\",\\\"mathlib_commit\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\",\\\"mathlib_root\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\"},\\\"inputs\\\":[]},\\\"graph\\\":{\\\"format_version\\\":2,\\\"case_id\\\":\\\"geometry-product-dimension\\\",\\\"spec_sha256\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\",\\\"propositions\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H001\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"E is nonempty.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"E\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H002\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"E is compact.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"E\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"M001\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"mathlib\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"For a set A in a Borel extended metric space and d≥0, if d<dim_H(A), then the d-dimensional Hausdorff measure of A is infinite.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"dim_H\\\"],\\\"source\\\":{\\\"statement\\\":\\\"hausdorffMeasure_of_lt_dimH: if (d:ℝ≥0)<dimH A then μH[d] A=∞.\\\",\\\"hypotheses\\\":[\\\"A set in an extended metric space with the Borel measurable structure required by Mathlib's hausdorffMeasure and dimH declarations; d is an NNReal.\\\"],\\\"evidence\\\":[{\\\"path\\\":\\\"library/M001-0001/library-sources.json\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"1e2974873151488a644ca1f93451e98bf2f2e911dba567adf7983fa7abfccdb1\\\"}],\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"hausdorffMeasure_of_lt_dimH\\\",\\\"module\\\":\\\"Mathlib.Topology.MetricSpace.HausdorffDimension\\\",\\\"mathlib_commit\\\":\\\"905b95818eb32af7874a58b427f50c1711a5e96c\\\",\\\"source_path\\\":\\\"Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/HausdorffDimension.lean\\\",\\\"source_sha256\\\":\\\"fdc61e7f179044cd714058f209b100e51b6f8af69aff295e3ee629ed45dcee31\\\",\\\"signature\\\":\\\"@hausdorffMeasure_of_lt_dimH.{u_1} : ∀ {X : Type u_1} [EMetricSpace X] [MeasurableSpace X] [BorelSpace X] {s : Set X} {d : NNReal}, (↑d < dimH s) → μH[d] s = ∞\\\",\\\"declaration_kind\\\":\\\"theorem\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"M002\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"mathlib\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"For a Lipschitz map f between extended metric spaces and any set A in its domain, dim_H(f '' A)≤dim_H(A).\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"dim_H\\\"],\\\"source\\\":{\\\"statement\\\":\\\"LipschitzWith.dimH_image_le: a Lipschitz map does not increase Hausdorff dimension of an image.\\\",\\\"hypotheses\\\":[\\\"X and Y are extended metric spaces; K:NNReal; f:X→Y is LipschitzWith K; s⊆X.\\\"],\\\"evidence\\\":[{\\\"path\\\":\\\"library/M002-0002/library-sources.json\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"24901487517562f47ec0d40b0915c250514f02599c40979d318f9d92bc9b804e\\\"}],\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"LipschitzWith.dimH_image_le\\\",\\\"module\\\":\\\"Mathlib.Topology.MetricSpace.HausdorffDimension\\\",\\\"mathlib_commit\\\":\\\"905b95818eb32af7874a58b427f50c1711a5e96c\\\",\\\"source_path\\\":\\\"Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/HausdorffDimension.lean\\\",\\\"source_sha256\\\":\\\"fdc61e7f179044cd714058f209b100e51b6f8af69aff295e3ee629ed45dcee31\\\",\\\"signature\\\":\\\"@LipschitzWith.dimH_image_le : ∀ {X Y} [EMetricSpace X] [EMetricSpace Y] {K:NNReal} {f:X→Y}, LipschitzWith K f → ∀ s:Set X, dimH(f '' s)≤dimH s\\\",\\\"declaration_kind\\\":\\\"theorem\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"M003\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"mathlib\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"For a finite-dimensional real normed space V and set A⊆V with nonempty interior, dim_H(A)=finrank(ℝ,V).\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"dim_H\\\"],\\\"source\\\":{\\\"statement\\\":\\\"Real.dimH_of_nonempty_interior: if a set in a finite-dimensional real normed space has nonempty interior, its Hausdorff dimension is the finrank of the space.\\\",\\\"hypotheses\\\":[\\\"V is a finite-dimensional real normed space and interior(A) is nonempty.\\\"],\\\"evidence\\\":[{\\\"path\\\":\\\"library/M003-0003/library-sources.json\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"c783a006ff20bfe97d7c98bfd5f18d8784ed298de1696686684d298de169668\\\"}],\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"Real.dimH_of_nonempty_interior\\\",\\\"module\\\":\\\"Mathlib.Topology.MetricSpace.HausdorffDimension\\\",\\\"mathlib_commit\\\":\\\"905b95818eb32af7874a58b427f50c1711a5e96c\\\",\\\"source_path\\\":\\\"Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/HausdorffDimension.lean\\\",\\\"source_sha256\\\":\\\"fdc61e7f179044cd714058f209b100e51b6f8af69aff295e3ee629ed45dcee31\\\",\\\"signature\\\":\\\"Real.dimH_of_nonempty_interior\\\",\\\"declaration_kind\\\":\\\"theorem\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"M004\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"mathlib\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"For a countable family of nonnegative measurable functions, the integral of their pointwise sum is the sum of their integrals.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[],\\\"source\\\":{\\\"statement\\\":\\\"lintegral_tsum: lintegral of a countable sum of nonnegative extended-real functions equals the sum of their lintegrals, provided every summand is almost-everywhere measurable.\\\",\\\"hypotheses\\\":[\\\"A measurable space with a measure; a countable index type; each summand is AEMeasurable into ENNReal.\\\"],\\\"evidence\\\":[{\\\"path\\\":\\\"library/M004-0005/library-sources.json\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"b0fd457ea61a6a025c9884af4cc4afcff3a4bb6a1649fcb7276fb23108a3a8ff\\\"}],\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"MeasureTheory.lintegral_tsum\\\",\\\"module\\\":\\\"Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.Lebesgue.Add\\\",\\\"mathlib_commit\\\":\\\"905b95818eb32af7874a58b427f50c1711a5e96c\\\",\\\"source_path\\\":\\\"Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Integral/Lebesgue/Add.lean\\\",\\\"source_sha256\\\":\\\"14da3dd3c269221e9ec43e91c6b22bb02d5db7f00e03c789661c72dffecf7b4a\\\",\\\"signature\\\":\\\"@MeasureTheory.lintegral_tsum : ∀ {α β} {m} {μ} [Countable β] {f:β→α→ENNReal}, (∀i, AEMeasurable (f i) μ) → ∫⁻ a, ∑'i,f i a ∂μ = ∑'i,∫⁻a,f i a ∂μ\\\",\\\"declaration_kind\\\":\\\"theorem\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"P\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"target\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"dim_H(E×I)=dim_H(E)+1.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"E\\\",\\\"I\\\",\\\"dim_H\\\"]}],\\\"inferences\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"R001\\\",\\\"inputs\\\":[\\\"H001\\\",\\\"H002\\\",\\\"M001\\\",\\\"M002\\\",\\\"M003\\\",\\\"M004\\\"],\\\"output\\\":\\\"P\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"rules\\\":[\\\"direct\\\",\\\"case_elimination\\\",\\\"forall_introduction\\\"],\\\"locals\\\":[],\\\"argument\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Write D=dim_H(E), F=E×[0,1], with distance squared |x−y|²+|t−u|². The compact set E is bounded in ℝ^n; covering a bounded Euclidean box by O(k^n) cubes of diameter O(1/k) shows H^q(E)=0 for every q>n, so D is finite. The threshold characterization then gives H^q(E)=0 whenever q>D. Fix q>D. At every scale δ≤1, choose a cover of E by sets of positive diameters r_j≤δ with arbitrarily small sum Σr_j^q. Zero-diameter members are singletons; replace each by a positive-diameter ball of diameter at most δ, choosing added q-cost summable and arbitrarily small. Cover I for each j by at most 1/r_j+1 intervals of length at most r_j. The corresponding products have diameter at most √2r_j and total (q+1)-cost at most 2(√2)^(q+1)Σr_j^q. Their maximum diameters tend to zero with δ, and cost tends to zero; hence H^(q+1)(F)=0 and dim_H(F)≤D+1.\\\",\\\"uses\\\":[\\\"H002\\\"],\\\"uses_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"E\\\",\\\"F\\\",\\\"D\\\",\\\"I\\\",\\\"n\\\"],\\\"produces\\\":[],\\\"introduces\\\":[],\\\"discharges\\\":[]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"S002\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"For the lower bound when D>0, fix 0<s<D. By M001, H^s(E)=∞. Consequently the scale-s contents c_s(E,δ) tend to infinity as δ decreases to zero: these contents are monotone as the scale decreases and their limit defines H^s. For an arbitrary countable cover V_i of F with ρ_i=diam(V_i)≤δ≤1, project to A_i⊆ℝ^n and B_i⊆I. Then diam(A_i),diam(B_i)≤ρ_i. Enlarge each B_i into an open interval J_i of length ≤ρ_i+η_i, with η_i>0 and Ση_iρ_i^s<ε. For every t∈I, the A_i for which t∈J_i cover E: for every x∈E, (x,t) belongs to some V_i, so t∈B_i⊆J_i. Thus c_s(E,δ)≤Σ_i 1_{J_i}(t)ρ_i^s pointwise. These interval indicators are measurable; Tonelli M004 and integration over I yield c_s(E,δ)≤Σ_i |J_i∩I|ρ_i^s≤Σ_iρ_i^(s+1)+ε. Terms with ρ_i=0 contribute zero since s>0. Let ε→0 and take the infimum over all product covers to obtain c_s(E,δ)≤c_(s+1)(F,δ). The left side tends to infinity as δ→0, so H^(s+1)(F)=∞ and M001's converse threshold implication (equivalently the definition of dim_H) gives dim_H(F)≥s+1. As this holds for every 0<s<D, dim_H(F)≥D+1.\\\",\\\"uses\\\":[\\\"M001\\\",\\\"M004\\\"],\\\"uses_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"E\\\",\\\"F\\\",\\\"D\\\",\\\"I\\\",\\\"s\\\",\\\"δ\\\",\\\"V_i\\\",\\\"ρ_i\\\",\\\"A_i\\\",\\\"B_i\\\",\\\"J_i\\\",\\\"η_i\\\",\\\"ε\\\",\\\"c_s\\\",\\\"H^s\\\"],\\\"produces\\\":[],\\\"introduces\\\":[],\\\"discharges\\\":[]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"S003\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"If D=0, choose x₀∈E using H001. The coordinate projection π:F→I, π(x,t)=t, is 1-Lipschitz by the displayed Euclidean distance and is onto because (x₀,t)∈F for each t. Its image has dimension 1: I has nonempty interior in ℝ, and M003 gives dim_H(I)=finrank(ℝ,ℝ)=1. Applying M002 to π and F gives 1=dim_H(I)≤dim_H(F)=D+1. Combining with the upper bound proves equality. This works unchanged when n=0, since E is then a nonempty subset of a singleton and π remains onto.\\\",\\\"uses\\\":[\\\"H001\\\",\\\"M002\\\",\\\"M003\\\"],\\\"uses_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"E\\\",\\\"F\\\",\\\"I\\\",\\\"x₀\\\",\\\"π\\\",\\\"D\\\",\\\"n\\\"],\\\"produces\\\":[],\\\"introduces\\\":[],\\\"discharges\\\":[]}],\\\"applications\\\":[{\\\"input\\\":\\\"M001\\\",\\\"at\\\":\\\"S002\\\",\\\"bindings\\\":{},\\\"hypothesis_checks\\\":[\\\"Apply to X=ℝ^n with its Euclidean Borel metric, A=E and real s>0 with s<D; thus s<dim_H(E) and the Hausdorff measure is infinite.\\\"]},{\\\"input\\\":\\\"M002\\\",\\\"at\\\":\\\"S003\\\",\\\"bindings\\\":{},\\\"hypothesis_checks\\\":[\\\"The coordinate map π has Lipschitz constant 1 for the concatenated Euclidean distance; the set is F.\\\"]},{\\\"input\\\":\\\"M003\\\",\\\"at\\\":\\\"S003\\\",\\\"bindings\\\":{},\\\"hypothesis_checks\\\":[\\\"Apply with V=ℝ and A=[0,1], whose interior contains (0,1); finrank(ℝ,ℝ)=1.\\\"]},{\\\"input\\\":\\\"M004\\\",\\\"at\\\":\\\"S002\\\",\\\"bindings\\\":{},\\\"hypothesis_checks\\\":[\\\"Use counting measure on I and the nonnegative measurable summands ρ_i^s·1_{J_i∩I}; each is measurable because J_i is open.\\\"]}]}]}}\"}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read an explicitly frozen task document by ID; no other local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"report_obstacle","description":"Stop this stage honestly on a substantive or suspected proof gap, unavailable source, or input conflict. JSON fields: status, location, explanation, basis, partial_progress. Status must be SUBSTANTIVE_GAP, SUSPECTED_GAP, SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE or INPUT_CONFLICT. Difficulty alone is not a mathematical error.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"obstacle_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["obstacle_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"probe_library","description":"Query a proved Mathlib theorem and its exact signature/axioms in the offline sandbox. Returns located evidence for an M source; the mathematical statement and applicability still require review.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"declaration":{"type":"string"},"module":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","declaration","module"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false}],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":false,"prompt_cache_key":"9064e1d1-e280-491d-84a7-d786523e760a","prompt_cache_retention":"24h","text":{"format":{"type":"text"},"verbosity":"low"},"top_p":0.98,"top_logprobs":0,"temperature":1.0,"reasoning":{"effort":"high","context":"all_turns","summary":null,"mode":"standard"},"user":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":35753,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3875,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":434},"total_tokens":39628,"attribution":{"items":{"fc_0ab345649bc6d74b016adb1f9deaa88191ac3d3b8ef4b0e007":{"input_tokens":31,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_0ab345649bc6d74b016adb1f9fd9508191b19d67217a45711a":{"input_tokens":34,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_0ab345649bc6d74b016adb1fa336048191a9fbdc13614c